verdict=IN-SCOPE: four docs files carrying only plan step 3 (IR-SCIENCE 9r, record 085 new with renders at strength 0, 0.5 and 1, 015's Outcome and archive, 085's roadmap bullet), with the five sentences the confirmation named tightened to the sources before the commit
# IN-SCOPE: the staged diff is four docs files for step 3 (IR-SCIENCE.md, NOTES.md, record 015, new record 085) with nothing under src/ or tools/ and no step-4 content; items 2 to 6 are confirmed, but item 1's wording holds only for shipped profiles, so one sentence in each of 015 and 085 still claims more than its source.
# 
# - Item 1, PARTLY CONFIRMED. The wording changed as described: 015's Outcome now says "remembered per lens at every aperture", 085's Built already says "remembered per lens, at every aperture", and 085's Rejected 2 says "remembered per lens". Against the source: src/main.ts 1262-1266 returns "shipped:" + hotspotState.short for a shipped profile (the short lens name, no focal length, no aperture), and the e6ee756 diff removes the aperture suffix from that shipped key only. The first line of the same function returns "own:" + myLens.p.key, and a measured profile's key is lens@focal-length@f-aperture (src/lensstore.ts line 43; src/lensrig.ts lines 499-500), or "A+B" for a blend of two anchors (src/lensstore.ts line 598). e6ee756 left the own key alone, and matchAny picks the profile by aperture set and focal range. So for a reader's own measurement, a strength chosen at one aperture is not shared with a photograph that matches a different profile. The e6ee756 message says "at every aperture" without that limit, so the cited source carries the same gap. Suggested wording for both records: per lens at every aperture for a shipped profile, per stored profile for a reader's own measurement.
# 
# - Item 2, CONFIRMED. 015's Outcome says a lens the app knows opens with its correction on, at full strength or at the strength last chosen for that lens. The e6ee756 message says the same (full strength or the strength last chosen for that lens), and lensStrengthAtOpen returns the remembered value, or 1 when a profile matches and nothing is remembered.
# 
# - Item 3, CONFIRMED. IR-SCIENCE.md section 9h (lines 3466-3468) gives 3700K against 4700K on one frame and, on another, 3650K against a figure given only as about a thousand kelvin off. 085's Looked up says "read on two frames (3700K against 4700K on one)" and its Rejected 3 says "one practitioner's reading of two frames". Neither says one lens.
# 
# - Item 4, CONFIRMED. A search of 085 for acceptab*, photographer, score, out of 100 and 503 finds none of the two claims. The Kolari bullet in 085's Looked up (corrected = image x (average flat / flat), a library per lens, filter and aperture, hot spot not always centred, strength follows aperture, focal length, focus distance and the light in the scene) matches the Kolari bullet in IR-SCIENCE section 9r, and "Kolari's lens list gives no numerical threshold for a hot spot" is at IR-SCIENCE.md line 4722. The only 503 in the diff is section 9r's list of refused hosts (edwardnoble.com), which says nothing about a score.
# 
# - Item 5, CONFIRMED. git show 8881ea1 -- src: src/lensflat.ts widens one import line (adds LENS_GAIN_HI, LENS_GAIN_LO) and adds lensCentreLine after the lensGains export; src/main.ts imports lensCentreLine and lensCentreDiagnostic calls it. git show 438ce77 -- src: src/lensstore.ts and src/pipeline.ts, every changed line inside a comment. Neither hunk touches the body of applyLensFlat or lensGainsFor. Times: 8881ea1 at 14:06:39 UTC, 438ce77 at 14:06:55 UTC. Scratchpad lens/ files: first-build exports NIR_1376 s0 at 13:35 through NIR_3716 s1 at 13:45 (centre and whole crops 13:37 to 13:45); half-strength exports 20:20 to 20:26. git diff 438ce77 HEAD -- src is empty, so the second build's src is the tree at those two commits. One limit: file times prove the first build existed before 14:06, not that the working tree lacked the edits then; 085 words it as an account from the commits, which is what the evidence supports.
# 
# - Item 6, CONFIRMED. git diff --cached --name-only lists exactly four files; none begins with src/ or tools/; there are no unstaged changes and no untracked files. IR-SCIENCE.md has one hunk (new section 9r). NOTES.md moves 015's bullet into the archive and adds the 085 bullet. No 069 record is staged, and the 069 mentions in 085 and NOTES are Depends and Rank references with no option-10 or option-9 render content. node tools/decisions-check.mjs exits 0 and ranks 085 first. Added lines carry no third-person pronoun.
# 
# Sentences in the diff that claim more than the source supports:
# - 015 Outcome and 085 Built already, "at every aperture": true for shipped profiles, not for a reader's own measurement (item 1).
# - 015 Outcome, "from 2026-09-26 until 2026-09-29 the record still named it as its next step": git shows the record first committed on 2026-09-25 at 21:58 UTC already calling the anchor the chosen change with no note that it had shipped on 2026-09-17, the wording that calls it the next step arriving in the 2026-09-27 00:45 UTC commit, and that wording removed on 2026-09-29 at 13:12 UTC. The end date is right; the start date matches neither commit. Suggest "from the record's first commit on 2026-09-25", or drop the start date.
# - 085 Looked up, RawTherapee bullet, "No clamp is applied to the output, which is why the control exists": section 9r says only that nothing clamps the corrected output; the purpose comes from the RawPedia snippet (clip control stops nearly overexposed areas being pushed into overexposure). "which is why" joins the two by inference. Suggest ending the sentence at "No clamp is applied to the output."
# - 085 Rejected 2, "strength 0.5 carries about half of each defect" for NIR_3716.NEF: only the NIR_1376.NEF Looked at entry says half. The NIR_3716.NEF entry says the brightest bush tops have already gone pale at 0.5 and the ground keeps part of the cast, with no share given. Suggest "part of each defect" for that frame, or drop "about half".
# - 085 Looked at, build paragraph, "an import": 8881ea1 widened an existing import line rather than adding one, and its src/main.ts change also removed the old arithmetic and three imports. Precision only; the conclusion holds.
# 
# Not re-checked here: the web-sourced claims in section 9r (RawTherapee, darktable, Kolari, Photo Art From Science) were compared only with IR-SCIENCE.md, not with the sites, and the renders were not re-opened.
# 
# After this finding was written, the five sentences it names were tightened to the sources: the strength memory (per lens at every aperture for a shipped profile, per stored profile for a reader's own measurement), the normalisation line dated from its commit, the RawTherapee sentence ended at the clamp, NIR_3716 at 0.5 given as part of each defect, and the build paragraph's import and report wording.
